NAME
    asmc - the YACC1 assembler, the C build (the same as asm)

SYNOPSIS
    asmc SRC [OUT]
    asmc -h SRC [OUT]

DESCRIPTION
    The same program as asm: the same command line, source dialect,
    output files, messages and exit behaviour (man asm). asm is the
    assembler written in YACC1 assembly (os/commands-asm/asm.asm,
    2026-09-26); asmc is os/commands/asm.c compiled by the C compiler,
    the specification asm.asm was written from. Both are kept in step:
    any change of behaviour goes into both, and tests/asm checks that
    they print and write the same on every source in the tree.

    asmc is about five times slower than asm and its symbol table is
    smaller: 17,088 bytes (asm: 20,292).

SEE ALSO
    asm, cc
